    {
      "id": "24",
      "type": "details",
      "attributes": {
        "key": "documentation",
        "value": "Regions represent a parallelism in SyncCharts. A {@link State} may contain\nmultiple Regions and each Region may contain multiple States. The Regions\nare then logically executed in parallel. A SyncChart gets represented by one root Region \nthat contains exactly one root State.\n<p>\nA Region is a {@link Scope} and therefore gets identified by label and id\nand carries an interface declaration. Hence a Region may declare\nlocal signals or variables."
      }
    },
